      "response": "We comprehensively address reliability with a four-layer defense: (1) ENSEMBLE VLM VERIFICATION: Instead of single-VLM annotation, we use 2-3 diverse VLMs (Qwen2.5-VL-72B, InternVL2.5-78B, Gemini-2.5-Flash) with majority vote. Using architecturally diverse VLMs (different vision encoders, different training data, different model families) ensures that systematic biases of one VLM are unlikely to be shared by all three. (2) DEDICATED PERCEPTION VERIFICATION: For the most critical category (perception errors), a separate targeted verification step extracts the specific visual claim and verifies it against the ground truth, rather than relying on holistic error classification. This reduces the false positive rate for the most important category. (3) CONFIDENCE-CALIBRATED LABELING: Annotations are binned into HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW confidence based on ensemble agreement. Only HIGH and MEDIUM labels are used automatically. The asymmetric default (uncertain labels default to reasoning error rather than perception error) protects the most critical category from contamination. (4) HUMAN-IN-THE-LOOP FOR LOW CONFIDENCE: The ~15-20% of samples with LOW confidence are routed to human annotators who see the image, solution step, and ensemble rationales. This produces both the final labels for difficult cases and a gold-standard calibration set for measuring the automated pipeline's accuracy. The gold-standard subset (5,000 fully human-annotated steps) enables precise measurement of per-category precision/recall for the automated pipeline, providing transparency about where the pipeline succeeds and fails.",
