      "response_artifacts": "MALR commits to releasing three concrete artifacts: (1) VisualPRM400K-Typed: the VL-PRM300K dataset re-annotated with 5-category error type labels (plus additional newly-annotated samples), with confidence scores and human verification flags for each label. This is the first large-scale multimodal PRM dataset with typed error labels. (2) MALR Annotation Pipeline: the full ensemble VLM annotation pipeline as an open-source tool, including prompt templates, confidence calibration code, cascade detection algorithms, and human annotation interface. This enables any research group to type-annotate their own multimodal PRM datasets. (3) VisualProcessBench-Typed: the VisualProcessBench evaluation benchmark extended with typed error labels, enabling standardized evaluation of error-type-aware PRMs.",
